{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Land dependabot PR #127 (uv-lock group) through Gerrit — pypandoc-binary 1.17 + ruff 0.16.2 only; mcp 2.0 stays deferred to 732b\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror for this project: dependabot keeps opening dependency PRs\nthere, but they can never merge — the content has to be re-applied locally and landed as a\nGerrit change, then the PR closed by hand. PR #127 (\"deps: bump the uv-lock group across 1\ndirectory with 3 updates\", branch `dependabot/uv/uv-lock-dd93acce05`) proposes three bumps:\n\n* `pypandoc-binary` `1.15` -> `1.17` — pinned EXACTLY in the `wiki` extra and the `dev`\n  group (the exact pin is deliberate: byte-safety tests assert byte-level pandoc output, so\n  local and CI must ship the identical binary).\n* `ruff` `0.16.1` -> `0.16.2` — pinned EXACTLY in the `dev` group (pre-commit hook, local\n  `make lint`, and CI must run the identical ruff).\n* `mcp` `1.29.0` -> `2.0.0` (major), with the pyproject ceiling loosened `<2` -> `<3` in\n  both the `mcp` and `dev` extras.\n\nThe `mcp` half is the THIRD re-proposal of the same major bump (PRs #124, #125, now #127).\nIt was investigated under ticket 1dfd (entodermic-dizzying-pikeperch) and rejected on\nevidence: mcp 2.0 removes the `mcp.server.fastmcp` module (verified `ModuleNotFoundError`)\nthat `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` and `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` import; the structural\nmigration (FastMCP -> MCPServer, transport params moved off the constructor, mcp-types\nsplit, sse-starlette >=3, lifespan/worker-thread/421 behavioral audits) is already tracked\nas its own open epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b` (bared-nickel-insect), \"Migrate MCP server to\nmcp 2.0 (fastmcp removal)\", whose migrate-vs-defer analysis explicitly recommends staying\non `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` until 2.0.x has patch releases. PR #125 applied the same path-2\ndecision rule (ticket carnivoral-consistent-lhasaapso, Gerrit change 1483). Re-litigating\nit here would duplicate 732b, so this ticket lands only the safe subset.\n\n## Approach\n\nLand the **safe subset** of PR #127 — the `pypandoc-binary` and `ruff` bumps — and leave\nthe `mcp` ceiling at `<2` so the resolver keeps `mcp` 1.29.0, consistent with tickets 1dfd\nand carnivoral-consistent-lhasaapso.\n\nConcretely, in a fresh worktree (`../deps-bump`) branched from current `origin/main`:\n\n1. Edit `pyproject.toml`: `\"pypandoc-binary==1.15\"` -> `\"pypandoc-binary==1.17\"` in BOTH\n   the `wiki` extra and the `dev` group (the notice test enforces a single distinct pin\n   value); `\"ruff==0.16.1\"` -> `\"ruff==0.16.2\"` in the `dev` group. Keep both pins exact.\n2. Refresh the lock with `uv lock --upgrade-package pypandoc-binary --upgrade-package ruff`\n   so `uv.lock` is regenerated by uv rather than hand-edited (CI gates on\n   `uv lock --check`). Then `uv sync` the dev environment so the new wheels are installed.\n3. **pandoc provenance (NOTICE)**: pypandoc-binary bumps change the BUNDLED pandoc\n   executable. Determine the new bundled version empirically\n   (`python -c \"import pypandoc; print(pypandoc.get_pandoc_version())\"`). If it differs\n   from 3.6.1, update `NOTICE` (the `Version:` line and the `pypandoc-binary==1.15` wheel\n   reference) and the version-string assertion in\n   `tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py` (the `\"3.6.1\" in text` line) so the GPL\n   provenance record matches what actually ships. Do NOT touch the upstream-URL assertion\n   (`\"pandoc.org\" in text or ...`) — a parallel change owns that exact line and the two\n   diffs must rebase cleanly past each other.\n4. **Byte-safety corpus (the load-bearing consumer of the shipped binary)**: the DC wiki\n   renderer's byte-compatibility baseline pins the installed pandoc exactly —\n   `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` freezes `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION = \"3.6.1\"`\n   and a per-platform `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` map (darwin-arm64 + linux-x86_64),\n   and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::`\n   `test_the_installed_pandoc_matches_the_legacy_fixture_provenance` validates the\n   installed binary's version + SHA-256 against the provenance embedded in\n   `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` and the three\n   `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_replay/` files. Bumping the wheel therefore requires\n   deliberately re-establishing the reviewed baseline, exactly as the generator's\n   docstring sanctions (\"Regenerate them only when intentionally establishing a reviewed\n   byte-compatibility baseline\"):\n   a. Update `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` to the new bundled version.\n   b. Recompute BOTH fingerprints: darwin-arm64 by SHA-256 of the locally installed\n      pandoc binary (`pypandoc.get_pandoc_path()`), and linux-x86_64 by downloading the\n      exact `pypandoc_binary` 1.17 manylinux x86_64 wheel recorded in `uv.lock` (URL +\n      hash pinned there), extracting it, and hashing the `pandoc` executable inside — no\n      Linux host required, and the wheel's integrity is attested by the uv.lock hash.\n   c. Regenerate the legacy manifest and the three replay files with\n      `python scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` under the new pin (the script\n      claims byte-identical output across supported binaries of the same version, so a\n      darwin regeneration is valid for CI's linux gate; the provenance test enforces this).\n   d. Confirm with the script's non-writing `--check` mode and the full\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py` module.\n   If the regenerated golden bytes churn implausibly (e.g. corpus-unit count deviates from\n   the expected 884 or `--check` disagrees after regeneration), STOP and defer the\n   pypandoc half too (landing ruff alone) rather than committing an unreviewed baseline.\n5. **ruff verdict drift**: ruff changes lint/format rules between releases. Run\n   `make lint`; if 0.16.2 flags existing code or reformats files, apply the minimal fix\n   and note it in the commit message. NEVER touch `.github/complexity-baseline.json`.\n6. Do NOT touch the `mcp` constraints, `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`, or ADR 0050 —\n   those are 732b's edit-set.\n7. Verify (`make lint && make typecheck`, `pytest tests/unit` — which includes the\n   wiki-renderer byte-safety/pandoc provenance tests — plus the generator's `--check`\n   pass), commit with a\n   `rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO sign-off, push `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`, and\n   leave the ticket `in_progress` while the orchestrator shepherds `LLM-Review` and\n   `Verified`; the ticket closes only after the change merges and PR #127 is closed with a\n   provenance comment pointing the mcp half at 732b.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `pyproject.toml` — the two `pypandoc-binary==` pins (`wiki` extra + `dev` group) and the\n  single `ruff==` pin in the `dev` group.\n* `uv.lock` — the regenerated `pypandoc-binary` and `ruff` entries plus whatever\n  incidental churn `uv lock` emits.\n* `NOTICE` + `tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py` — only if the bundled pandoc\n  version changed (expected), and never the upstream-URL assertion line.\n* `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` — `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` and both\n  `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` entries, nothing else in the script.\n* `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` and the three files under\n  `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_replay/` — regenerated wholesale by the generator, never\n  hand-edited.\n* Minimal source fixes ONLY if ruff 0.16.2 changes a lint/format verdict on existing code.\n* OUT: the `mcp` 1.29.0 -> 2.0.0 bump and its `<2` -> `<3` ceiling move (deferred to epic\n  `732b-51df-acf2-477b` / bared-nickel-insect — already filed, so no new ticket is needed);\n  `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`; ADR 0050; `.github/complexity-baseline.json`;\n  dependabot configuration; any other open dependency PR.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `pyproject.toml` contains `pypandoc-binary==1.17` (twice: `wiki` + `dev`) and\n  `ruff==0.16.2`, and still contains `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` in both the `mcp` extra and the\n  `dev` group — checked with `grep -nE 'pypandoc-binary==|ruff==|mcp>=' pyproject.toml`.\n- [ ] AC2: `uv.lock` records `pypandoc-binary` at `1.17`, `ruff` at `0.16.2`, and `mcp`\n  at `1.29.0` — checked with `grep -A1 -E '^name = \"(pypandoc-binary|ruff|mcp)\"$' uv.lock`\n  — and `uv lock --check` exits 0 (the same gate CI runs).\n- [ ] AC3: `NOTICE` names the pandoc version actually bundled by pypandoc-binary 1.17\n  (verified empirically via `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()` in the synced worktree venv)\n  and references `pypandoc-binary==1.17`; `pytest tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py`\n  exits 0.\n- [ ] AC4: the byte-safety baseline is re-established coherently: `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION`\n  and both `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` fingerprints in the generator match the 1.17\n  wheels (darwin hash from the installed binary, linux hash from the uv.lock-pinned\n  manylinux x86_64 wheel), the legacy manifest + replay fixtures are regenerated by the\n  script (not hand-edited), `python scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py --check`\n  exits 0, and `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py` exits 0\n  (including the provenance test) on the new binary.\n- [ ] AC5: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` exits 0 in the worktree under\n  ruff 0.16.2, `make typecheck` exits 0, and `pytest tests/unit` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC6: A Gerrit change carrying this diff exists on refs/for/main with this ticket's\n  `rebar-ticket:` trailer and a DCO sign-off — checked with `git log -1 --format=%B HEAD`\n  and the Gerrit change URL printed by the push.\n- [ ] AC7: The mcp 2.0 half is NOT landed: no edit to the `mcp` constraints, and the\n  deferral is recorded as a comment on this ticket naming epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b` —\n  checked by `git diff origin/main --stat` showing no `_optionality.yml`/ADR-0050 change\n  and `rebar show <this>` showing the comment."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786805149845929001,"uuid":"e616736c-2ef9-4b92-9669-64355e5c0622"}